      {
        "id": "p26-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z&=10\\\\y+z&=7\\\\y-z&=3\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=6,\\ y=5,\\ z=2$.\n\nAdd the last two equations, then substitute.",
          "worked": "Adding the last two equations:\n$$\\begin{align*}(y+z)+(y-z)&=7+3\\\\2y&=10\\\\y&=5\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $y+z=7$:\n$$\\begin{align*}5+z&=7\\\\z&=2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the first equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2(5)-3(2)&=10\\\\x+4&=10\\\\x&=6\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $6+2(5)-3(2)=10$, $5+2=7$ and $5-2=3$.\nThus $x=6,\\ y=5,\\ z=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+y+z&=6\\\\2x+3y+4z&=20\\\\3x-2y+2z&=5\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,\\ y=2,\\ z=3$.\n\nEliminate $x$ from two pairs of equations, then substitute.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3), in order.\n$(2)-2(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x+3y+4z)-2(x+y+z)&=20-12\\\\y+2z&=8\\end{align*}$$\n$(3)-3(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x-2y+2z)-3(x+y+z)&=5-18\\\\-5y-z&=-13\\\\5y+z&=13\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract $5y+z=13$ from five times $y+2z=8$:\n$$\\begin{align*}5(y+2z)-(5y+z)&=40-13\\\\9z&=27\\\\z&=3\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y+2(3)&=8\\\\y&=2\\\\x+2+3&=6\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $1+2+3=6$, $2(1)+3(2)+4(3)=20$ and $3(1)-2(2)+2(3)=5$.\nThus $x=1,\\ y=2,\\ z=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 125
      }
    ]
  },
